756,37591,28,19,280,7633,7,68004,1188,15,11,15,701,19,11,16,5905,4038,7,68004,1188,15,11,18,701,17,11,16,14,17,1106,7633,54934,18,13,24,22,17515,16,29621,4080,16,13,24,22,11,18,13,16,29776,13268,18,13,24,22,17515,16,29621,7,16,13,24,22,11,18,13,16,3237,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe truncated right circular cone below has a large base radius 8 cm and a small base radius of 4 cm. The height of the truncated cone is 6 cm.  The volume of this solid is $n \\pi$ cubic cm, where $n$ is an integer.  What is $n$? [asy]\nimport olympiad; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); dotfactor=4;\ndraw(ellipse((0,0),4,1)); draw(ellipse((0,3),2,1/2));\ndraw((-3.97,.1)--(-1.97,3.1)^^(3.97,.1)--(1.97,3.1));\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"d77673ac81e063caf3c332a801daab5e27b18ea42a6c6b1ff5c28df7b5279c9b"},"seconds":9.343639373779297,"seed":953786399817129317,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the volume of the truncated right circular cone, we use the formula for the volume of a truncated cone:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi h (R^2 + Rr + r^2)\n\\]\nwhere \\(R\\) is the radius of the larger base, \\(r\\) is the radius of the smaller base, and \\(h\\) is the height of the truncated cone.\n\nGiven:\n- \\(R = 8\\) cm\n- \\(r = 4\\) cm\n- \\(h = 6\\) cm\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi \\cdot 6 \\cdot (8^2 + 8 \\cdot 4 + 4^2)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate the squares and the product:\n\\[\n8^2 = 64\n\\]\n\\[\n8 \\cdot 4 = 32\n\\]\n\\[\n4^2 = 16\n\\]\n\nNext, add these values together:\n\\[\n8^2 + 8 \\cdot 4 + 4^2 = 64 + 32 + 16 = 112\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute back into the volume formula:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi \\cdot 6 \\cdot 112\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n\\[\nV = \\frac{1}{3} \\pi \\cdot 672\n\\]\n\nFinally, multiply:\n\\[\nV = 224 \\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the truncated cone is \\(224 \\pi\\) cubic cm. Therefore, the integer \\(n\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{224}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{224}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"geometry:89"}
